531 0 obj
<<
/Title (Open bracket function, close bracket. Inside, if gs dot hasRole admin, return true. If gs dot hasRole bb1, return true. Otherwise return false. This script means, if the user is admin, allow full access. If the user has bb1 role, allow access, but the data condition will filter only EEE records. For all others, deny.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 533 0 R
/Next 528 0 R
>>
endobj
532 0 obj
<<
/Title (In any real organization, like a college, data security is very important. For example, a student or faculty from the EEE department should not be able to see the records of ECE or CSE departments.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 530 0 R
/Next 534 0 R
>>
endobj
533 0 obj
<<
/Title (And in the Script field, write this script:)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 535 0 R
/Next 531 0 R
>>
endobj
534 0 obj
<<
/Title (But by default in ServiceNow, if a user has access to a table, he can see all records. That is a security risk.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 532 0 R
/Next 536 0 R
>>
endobj
535 0 obj
<<
/Title (Now in Data Condition, set Branch is EEE.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 537 0 R
/Next 533 0 R
>>
endobj
536 0 obj
<<
/Title (So the purpose of this project is to implement record-level security using Script-Controlled Access Control List, or ACL. We will create a condition where only users who have the EEE branch role can view records where the Branch field is EEE. At the same time, the system admin will retain full access to all records, irrespective of the branch.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 534 0 R
/Next 538 0 R
>>
endobj
537 0 obj
<<
/Title (In the Requires role related list, add bb1.)
